The sing-box build used here carries a small set of patches, documented in that
repository's MODIFICATIONS.md. They exist because sing-box constructs an
inbound's user set once, at startup, and never exposes a way to change it; the
patches surface the update method its underlying services already have, so that
adding or removing a user does not require restarting a listener and dropping
every live connection.

